ance, reused input/endpoints and lossless local extraction are distinct origins.','NF-07 consumes existing art; it adds no provider execution, artistic approval, fresh Claude qualification or general engine support. Manifest creation accepted:false remains distinct from observed current eligibility.','Counts apply to bounded assignments and exact retained kits, not reliability rates. Human acceptance is unrecorded; milestones remain open.');prior_failures=(Refs @('evidence/domain-art-revision/20261112/production-01/specialist-raw-review.json','evidence/domain-art-revision/20261112/production-01/extraction-layout-failure.json','evidence/domain-consumers/20261112/claude-01/grade-01.json','evidence/native-production/20261112/claude-01/grade-01.json','evidence/native-production/20261112/claude-01-resume-01/grade-03.json','evidence/deliverable-index/20261114/cold-01/independent-01.json'))}
$a3=@{id='gaps';conclusion='No broad native update/relocation continuation qualification is established. INSTALL-SUPPORT qualifies five recorded local environment rows, copied-kit replacement and cold reads/moves, plus separate Windows host loading/local retrieval. SC-06 four consumer replays after same-path replacement are local compatibility proof. Relocation resumes artifacts in a new process; it does not prove an old conversation or child resumed. CF-10 has one explicitly guided runtime-upgrade recovery, which does not qualify broader update/move continuation. The capability matrix class-material reports no retained actual normal-map/VFX provider-and-renderer outcome; class-rig reports no assembled native rig or engine import/animation outcome.';evidence=(Refs @('docs/INSTALL-SUPPORT.md','docs/CAPABILITY-OUTCOMES.md','evidence/schema-compatibility/20261113/consumer-upgrade-01/result.json','evidence/native-production/20261112/claude-01-resume-02/grade-02.json'));limits=@('Passing local checks of normal orientation, material-channel isolation or companion alignment do not establish actual consumer material response, channel conventions, alpha/blending or effect quality.','Rig hierarchy/pivot/snap/budget checks do not establish attachment coordinates, occlusion, transform order, part replacement or animated seams in an assembled rig.','Fresh wheel installs and moved-consumer cold reads do not qualify in-place pip upgrades, relocated virtual environments, native continuation or provider access.','The recorded setup/install kit bindings are now stale; newer full verification does not replay those native cases.');prior_failures=@()}
$a4=@{id='applicability';conclusion='Receipt integrity and present applicability are separate. Exact retained passing bytes remain a historical pass when current sources, inventory, package or reviewed prose differ from tested bindings; this is a qualification gap, not demonstrated runtime regression. CURRENT-FULL-VERIFICATION is a stable registry ID pinned to older SC-06, not a moving newest-checkpoint pointer. NF-07-FULL-VERIFICATION binds the latest full checkpoint at evidence/verification-runs/20261114T152255.619054Z/result.json: 1393 passes, three Windows privilege skips, 39 reference checks and distribution checks. The fresh read-only inspection matches the retained report: 17 claims/57 receipts, only NF-07-CONSUMER and NF-07-FULL-VERIFICATION current; eleven historical; CORE-SETUP, CORE-INSTALL-UPDATE, CURRENT-FULL-VERIFICATION and CURRENT-CLAIM-REVIEW stale. Overall needs_review/exit 1 can coexist with an intact current selected claim and bundle. Recheck from the repository using .venv/Scripts/python.exe -B scripts/check_integrity.py --json, optionally repeated --claim ID filters. This reads identities without rebuilding or replaying evidence.';evidence=(Refs @('docs/EVIDENCE-INTEGRITY.md','evaluations/evidence-claims.json','evidence/deliverable-index/20261114/integrity-02/report.json','evidence/verification-runs/20261114T152255.619054Z/result.json'));limits=@('Fresh inspection stdout is saved separately in this scratch workspace at work/integrity-report.json; it is not a repository artifact.','Claim filtering still performs retained release checks, so overall exit 1 need not mean the selected claim is stale.','Integrity does not rerun tests, native hosts, provider calls or rendering, authenticate a provider, judge art, or confer human acceptance. Do not rebuild or change expected hashes merely to clear the report.');prior_failures=@()}
